#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Frozen reader for preregistration 0020 — real-content fit at 4096: does the encoder signal exist in
real files at all?

Written and committed BEFORE any fit was made under this preregistration.

WHY THIS EXISTS. 0018/0019 read OOB_TRANSFER_FAILS: 0014's searched HGB M4, fitted on the corpus
builder's eight generated families, identifies the encoder on five pinned real-file families at 0.0637
(2450 of 38452 rows) against 3402 needed. That reading cannot tell a training-distribution failure from
real content carrying little signal, because the model had never seen a real file. This run changes
exactly one thing: what the recipes are fitted on. Three recipes are fitted on a real-content corpus
built from the chunks of the same pinned files 0018's sealed evaluation corpus does not use
(tools/pivot/corpus_realfit.py), a fourth arm fits the headline recipe on the same number of the
builder's pool rows, a reproduction rung must reproduce 0003's banked 0.1965, and a null control must
sit at chance. Every fit is scored exactly once on 0018's scoring set, row for row.

This reader takes the runner's artifact (tools/pivot/run_realfit.py) and checks, clause by clause: the
sealed corpora (array hashes for the builder cache, the evaluation corpus and the fit corpus); the
sealed split and the three sealed fit blocks (hash for hash); that nothing scored was fitted (the
runner's measured chunk, source-chunk and row-identity counts must all be 0); that every fit is the
sealed recipe on the sealed rows with the sealed seed, scored exactly once, in the sealed order, with
its checkpoint fingerprint recomputed here; that each record's own scores equal what its per-example
vector gives; that the reproduction rung lands within 0.005 of 0.1965; that the null control sits at
chance on both row sets; and that every banked reading equals what this reader recomputes. Then one
clause: real_model's count of correct rows over the five real-file families against chance + 0.05.
REAL_FIT_CLEARS or REAL_FIT_FAILS, published at the same size; VOID on any validity failure.

NOT A TRANSFER READING. The fit chunks and the scored chunks are cut from the same five pinned blobs.
They share no byte, no chunk index, no chunk id and no source-chunk hash, and the runner measures that
rather than assuming it — but they are the same files, so a pass says the signal is reachable when the
model has seen content of that kind, not that it would be reachable on a file kind never seen. Every
verdict string this reader emits says so.

Digest convention: sha256 of np.ascontiguousarray(a).tobytes(); index arrays int64 in grouped_split /
np.nonzero order; sorted sets np.sort(...).astype(np.int64); corpus arrays as stored (float32 X, int16
y, int32 g little-endian, int8 fam); per-example vectors as int8 bytes.
"""
